  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered"><span class="username">Chamilka</span>, You Are The <span class="archetype">Ruler</span> - <span class="text-orange">And This Is What It Means...</span></h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/it-means.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>Your archetype suggests that you're an individual who possess great mental strength, fortitude, and an unbreakable sense of perseverance. You are never fearful of what the future holds for you, and you're always willing to step up to challenges of any sort.</p>
              <p>Yes, the Hero archetype is best represented through the <span class="text-orange">essence of sacrifice</span>. Whether it's putting the needs of others in front of your own, or simply taking the initiative to serve the greater good, you're always in the front of the line.</p>
              <p>That specific trait about you stems from your deep-seated instincts... Instincts that forbid you from retreating in the face of adversity. Instincts that prevent you from laying still in the face of injustice.</p>
              <p>While others prefer to sit on the sidelines, that's just not in your interests. That is also why it is often said, that the Hero has no fears... But let's address that in greater detail as we progress through this Archetypal Introduction.</p>
              <p>Your archetype also suggests that there is a side of you that's relentless... Relentless in the sense of striving to improve yourself - whether it's your physical abilities, your mental fortitude, or your emotional resilience.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>That being said, you're certainly an individual of impressive characteristics - characteristics that are unique to your archetype.</p>
          <p>You seem to <span class="text-orange">exercise selflessness in everything that you do</span>... No matter how small or minuscule your actions appear to be, every decision that you make, no matter how small, is always for a purpose that serves others. And when it comes to making important and difficult decisions, you're assertive, firm, and steadfast.</p>
          <p>Your archetype also suggests that you're an individual of great empathy, and a strong sense of justice.</p>
          <p>You're intolerant when you encounter unfairness or corruption of any sort, and there's burning desire that drives you to want to do all forms of prejudice.</p>
          <p>Your instinctive sense of righteousness is constantly pushing you to be better, to do more, and to try harder...</p>
          <p>You might not like to admit it... But from time to time, you do get worn out. After all, being a hero is certainly not a task for the weak and feeble. It can be emotionally and physically draining most of the time.</p>
          <p>As difficult or as impossible as it sounds, you must learn to prioritize your own rejuvenation.</p>
          <p>The Hero archetype is also one that <span class="text-orange">strives for greatness</span>. You have a strong vision of what you want to achieve in your lifetime - a vision that few will comprehend, but many will appreciate... Your compassion for your fellow man is what ultimately gives you the desire to change the world.</p>
          <p>You're an individual of great principles, character, and morals. Unlike the archetypes who tend to struggle with temptations and might struggle differentiating between right and wrong, you always have a clear idea of what is virtuous.</p>
          <p>You might not be aware of this, <span class="username"></span>... But your willingness to step up to the plate is inspiring and encouraging to the people around you - strangers, friends, and loved ones. And because of this, your archetype truly has the capacity to achieve greatness.</p>
          <p>That's why the world needs more people like you... I have no doubt that you will one day make a lasting impact on humanity, and contribute great things to the world.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Hero</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Qualities, Unknown Tendencies,<br>And Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>One of your prime qualities is your extroversion. You tend to be quite mobile in your social interaction with others, shuffling from person to person. And yet, you also tend to make an impression on all of them. You have a <span class="text-orange">charismatic aura</span> about you and a natural desire for partnership and companionship that the inevitable outcome is that you end up being more endeared to them in some way.</p>
              <p>As a Hero, there exists a bit of selfishness in you. This doesn’t necessarily mean that you’re going to be absolutely greedy and incapable of sharing with others. However, there may be times where you end up being quite an opportunist, bypassing even the benefit of others if it means personal glory on your part. Your honor, nonetheless, keeps you tempered and allows you to approach life cleanly, however deep the temptation might be.</p>
              <p>On the brighter side, you tend to have a more rational, objective mindset. This is because you want to see solutions, and you want to approach things in a predictable way. Much like the adventure of a hero, you want to <span class="text-orange">emulate the stories of those who have come before you</span>, and therefore want to structure your life in a predictable pattern. Whether or not you’ll succeed is something only time can ultimately tell, but there’s no doubt you are headed somewhere with your mind.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Your mind is a turbulent one, meaning that it is constantly active and searching for something to do. In a positive way, you are certainly someone who will bring cheer and energy into a group. However, there is also the potential for negativity and restlessness within you. </p>
          <p>This is normal, because the journey to being a true hero often involves internal turmoil. The fact that you have this archetype therefore means you’re already in the journey, and much like a real hero, you have strengths and weaknesses you will need to address.</p>
          <p>That being said, there’s more about your potential than you understand at this juncture, <span class="username"></span>. </p>
          <p>With your hidden qualities in full view, it is time for you to know what your strengths are and how you can better use them...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-1" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(1,2)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step2">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Hero, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Strengths And<br>Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities-2.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>As a Hero, you are full of energy and spirit. You are endlessly passionate about the things you believe in and protective of your legacy, as well as that of others. Your extroverted nature allows you to lighten up the mood simply by being yourself.</p>
              <p>Unlike other archetypes, the Hero does not need to talk or even make contact with other people to inspire them. As a result, you are perfectly capable of doing this on your own because courage is something that all of humanity can relate to. <span class="text-orange">Your energy exudes courage</span>, which in turn gives people hope.</p>
              <p>Thus, you will find that people are drawn to you in some way. Once you get to know people, some of them will stay and be lifelong friends, as though forming a main cast together with the powerful protagonist. As you take center stage, your courage and discipline will attract enough people to hopefully share the spotlight with you.</p>
              <p>Since you are a Hero, you are <span class="text-orange">often at a crossroads</span> and always made to choose between multiple options. You feel that there is so much freedom, but also that there is so much at stake. </p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>However, this is exactly what makes you decisive. Ordinary people would be overwhelmed by the sheer number of options they have in life, but you are willing to take risks and make leaps of faith because you find fulfillment in both the adventure and the rewards that come with it.</p>
          <p>This decisiveness attracts people to your cause and makes them recognize the kind of person that you are. When you make choices, you become an inspiration-- a model for those who have a hard time doing so. You inspire people to make tough choices of their own, such that they become Heroes themselves through your decision-making. </p>
          <p>As heroes learn new skills and overcome their barriers, they are able to solve problems more quickly over time. This is why efficiency is the hallmark of a Hero. </p>
          <p>Your mind is like a knife with this approach-- cutting straight to the point and removing any non-essentials factors. You are able to think about matters <span class="text-orange">logically and calmly</span>, and you will often leave your personal attachments behind as you think of solutions to your problems. </p>
          <p>Your mind is also endlessly curious about everything. The more you are able to learn new things, the easier it is for you to learn in general, as you become wiser and smarter with every new life skill or knowledge learned. As such, you should always find ways to sharpen the blade that is your mind. Read, watch, and talk to people to hone your mind further.</p>
          <p>The turbulence of your personality means that you will sometimes be extremely passionate or even obsessed about something. In the Hero’s case, it’s strength. The Hero archetype thrives when you are in a position of strength and often falters at the first sign of weakness.</p>
          <p>As such, you naturally <span class="text-orange">commit yourself to self-improvement</span>. For you, self-improvement is a means for you to constantly stay ahead of your own weaknesses. The more you learn and fail at learning new things, the more motivated you become. You are always asking yourself tough questions with the intent of self-improvement.</p>
          <p>Of course, this doesn’t mean that you are able to keep it together at all times, particularly when you remember the past. While you are able to improve in strategy, it may be harder for you to commit to emotional and spiritual self-improvement due to the psychological toll it often takes to achieve these. When confronted with situations like this, you need to stay strong and acknowledge that this is for your betterment.</p>
          <p>Now that you’re acquainted with your strengths, dear <span class="username"></span>, it is time for you to know how you can exercise them in various aspects of your life. </p>
          <p>For now, let’s start with one that strikes a chord: your romantic relationships.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-2" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(2,3)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5" id="step3">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Hero, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Relationship Qualities</span> That Are Within You</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/relationship.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>Due to your egocentric nature, you do not settle for anything less. Whereas other archetypes tend to be open and intuitive, you are inclined to idealism and ability. </p>
              <p>When you are in a relationship, this tendency will bring standards. As such, you may focus on the merit of the person you are with, and you may concern yourself further with either molding them into shape or constantly challenging them to be the best partner for you.</p>
              <p>Given this, you are likely to <span class="text-orange">look at romance from a consequentialist standpoint</span>. How much will this relationship benefit you and the other person? How will you two grow together? Will there be harmony in the relationship or disorder?</p>
              <p>When facing the worst of life together, you tend to expect the other person to step up and focus on getting things done. This doesn’t mean that you’re sidelining emotion, but you are also too aware that nothing happens, you bicker. You will seek efficiency even in love, and the right person will be all too happy to oblige.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>However, while this decision to <span class="text-orange">focus more on rationality and ability</span> is ultimately a good one, this arrangement can potentially strip away the emotional aspect if you are not careful.</p>
          <p>As a Hero, you need to infuse the relationship with the same emotional drive that you provide other people. In other words, while you can indeed be the Hero, you should also focus on being an authentic human being. </p>
          <p>Don’t let the relationship simply be about what works and what doesn’t. Instead, make it a relationship that allows having fun and simply being together. There’s always plenty of time to be rational, but just relax and have fun with your significant other when things aren’t happening. Don’t make it too robotic. Instead, make the relationship authentic.</p>
          <hr class="dashed">
          <p>Looking at the core qualities of your archetype, we’ll see a Hero who has journeyed, tried, and failed to look for the right person. This means that you will often be the more experienced one in the relationship.</p>
          <p>This trait often manifests in your likelihood to <span class="text-orange">measure relationships in terms of what they are worth</span>. To you, happiness in a relationship can only happen if the conditions are just right. A relationship is much like your own home-- it has to be at just the right spot before you can begin building one.</p>
          <p>When you look at your uncompromising attitude in terms of your own experiences, you begin to realize why you act exactly the way you do. You ultimately just want to protect the relationship and be its Hero. To this end, you will do everything to make sure that everything is in order before you can begin.</p>
          <p>As a result of this, however, the line between mentor and lover might initially get blurry since your experiences will likely force you to tell the person you love about what you expect from them. For the other person, this can be seen as wrongly domineering, when in reality, it is simply a kindness on your part.</p>
          <p>For this reason, it is typically advisable for the Hero to mingle with archetypes that can either tolerate and understand their behavior, such as the Caregiver or Jester, or happily satisfy the Hero’s immense standards, such as the Ruler.</p>
          <p>In either scenario, what will likely happen is that the two of you will steer each other towards a better relationship. Sometimes, <span class="text-orange">it will be competitive</span>, and other times it will seem like only one person is carrying the relationship. But as long as you have an eye for each other and love each other just as equally, your relationship can still blossom.</p>
          <p>As you know, however, the Hero is not just about romance and love. Indeed, there’s another aspect in your life where you can apply yourself, <span class="username"></span>. </p>
          <p>Without further ado, it’s time to see where you can take yourself in your career.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-3" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(3,4)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step4">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Hero</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Potential Career Paths</span></h3>
          </div>
          <p>Generally, the Hero is a combination of extroversion, egocentrism, rationality, and turbulence. This makes up for strong career paths in relation to rescue work, essential services, and law. With their protective nature, Heroes will undoubtedly find themselves at home with these jobs. And while these are suggestive of what you can pursue with your strengths, know that you should never limit yourself to them.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/emergency-rescue.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Emergency Rescue/Firefighter/Policemen</h5>
              <p>With their uniqueness, Heroes are best suited as protectors. Because they have the natural knack to defend what is good, they’ll find it natural to protect the lives of others.</p>
              <p>As a Hero, your gift is to help others live a full life. And what better way to do this apart from being in a position to save others when it matters most? In rescuing others, you will be fulfilling your natural desire to protect others from the evils that might come after them.</p>
              <p>One trait that allows you to fit the bill is your own natural bravery. Make no mistake, you are still nervous by the idea of having to rescue someone, saving property or defending them from evildoers. But you have enough guts to realize that society needs a shield to continue thriving.</p>
              <p>As such, even in the greatest moments of fear, when your personal courage is severely tested, you will be able to approach the dangers of life calmly and rationally. Fire, crime and other calamities may deter most people, but by the time you finally start doing your part, you will realize that you are brave enough to prevent these from hurting others. Your own will is unbendable enough already-- and with the right cause, what can stop you?</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>That besides, because of your extroverted nature, you would be a great addition to any team. Your presence will serve to calm the nerves of anyone new, and your extroversion will allow you to connect with them and pinpoint their fears. This will ensure that you will not only get along famously, but you will keep them up and eager to face any challenges in life.</p>
          <p>The jobs above will also help you temper your obstinacy as they will force you to work together with others. Though you are the protagonist in your story, plenty of other people will share in the tale, and because of that, you will be inclined to work with them even through the toughest of trials. Your prideful streak will be molded into true inner strength.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/health-worker.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Health Worker</h5>
              <p>Being a Hero isn’t just about conquering something or someone. In fact, that’s just one of the many misconceptions about being a Hero. It’s also about protecting a life-- saving it from anything that could endanger it. For this reason, working with the Health industry might be your cup of tea.</p>
              <p>There is already a lot that you can bring to the table on your own. You have a lot of energy for one, so you’re almost always going to be at your physical peak. This energy is furthered by your decisiveness and efficiency. Every action you take will not be wasted and will always be towards saving other people’s lives.</p>
              <p>More than that, the Health industry is vast, and there’s plenty of ways that you can help others. You can choose a particular specialization that appeals to your intellectual curiosity to further your career and expertise and then channel that curiosity into finding cures for diseases or distributing them whenever needed.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>The Health industry is also full of social interaction between clients and employees-- between the sick and the healer-- between the Hero and those being saved. These interactions will be your chance to forge friendships and protect both people’s health and their resolve to continue living.</p>
          <p>More than that, however-- your natural propensity for camaraderie will make you fit in nicely with your colleagues. Being fueled by your mutual passion to help others should be more than enough of a glue to hold your friendship together, but there’s always more that you can do together-- and your extroversion will help light the way.</p>
          <p>As a consequence, this career path allows you to live out your gift of bringing joy and happiness to others. You will be saving lives, and with them, the opportunity of others to continue bringing joy to this world and making it better.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/lawyer.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Lawyer</h5>
              <p>Heroes do not just protect people-- they also protect ideas, concepts like the rule of law. They protect the integrity of the State and the people from whom whose power and existence it emanates. Thus, one of the best jobs a Hero could have lies in the protection of the rule of law and the innocent.</p>
              <p>As a Hero, you have a propensity for rigidity in your thoughts and a desire to stick to your guns. This is an attitude that the law appreciates most. After all, it is in defense of principles and the innocent that one maintains the concept of civilization, nationhood, and justice. Without people of your gumption, the law cannot survive, and without law, none of the things we take for granted would exist.</p>
              <p>On a more practical note, the law is a fantastic springboard for politics, furthering your career and helping your people at the same time. Appreciating it thoroughly and knowing the ins and outs of maintaining the State is crucial if you want to help out other people. You can fight injustice not just through the courts, but by policy, and by constantly using the law to bring out true justice and fairness.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Your extroversion will also give you another advantage: bravery. You aren’t scared to face audiences or conduct business with people of far greater standing. By tethering yourself to the call of the law, you will tether yourself to a lot of people with wisdom, experience, and connections. You will be able to defend people or make deals with your powers of persuasion.</p>
          <p>As such, it’s easy to see why you would make a good lawyer. Not only do you have the traits for it, but even some of your weaknesses can also serve as your source of strength. This is truly a challenge worth undertaking, and glory will be had if you try hard enough.</p>
          <p>But while your career prospects certainly glimmer with the hope of prosperity, there are uncomfortable truths about yourself that you will need to face. The first of which will be no more comforting, <span class="username"></span>, and it is this...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-4" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(4,5)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
